# Checklist maintenance

When you **start from** a checklist or numbered task doc (for example [`docs/DEV_TASKS.md`](docs/DEV_TASKS.md)), treat updating that doc as part of the same deliverable as the code.

- As soon as an item is fully completed, immediately mark it completed (for example, change `- [ ]` to `- [x]`) and refresh any progress counts or summaries in the same file.
- Do not defer checklist updates to “after push” or the end of the session unless the user explicitly asked only for a draft.
- Do not batch many checklist updates until the very end if items finish at different times—mark each when it is done.
- Never tell the user a checklist item is done while the repo checklist still shows it incomplete.

If there is no checklist file for the work, this rule does not require inventing one.
